["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/LifecycleScopeType/decommission", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A relationship has specific context implications for a product's retirement and/or decommissioning.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nc6a25023c6a442cf95e6134be6b005fc", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:N3f7489cb99b74bbabaa72fb9d9d97236", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A reference to a Vulnerability Exploitability eXchange (VEX) statement which provides information on whether a product is impacted by a specific vulnerability in an included package and, if affected, whether there are actions recommended to remediate. See also [NTIA VEX one-page summary](https://ntia.gov/files/ntia/publications/vex_one-page_summary.pdf).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N23e149c6b879485381049a9d4878503d", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#class", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Extension/CdxPropertyEntry", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:N74bfb64122a041199498cf50f88912be", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose/executable", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ecli", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[European Case Law Identifier (ECLI)](https://data.europa.eu/data/datasets/european-case-law-identifier-ecli) is a uniform identifier for judicial decisions across Europe. It consists of five mandatory components: the \"ECLI\" prefix, a country code, a court code, the year of the decision, and a unique serial number (e.g., `ECLI:EU:C:2023:94`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/EnergyUnitType/other", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/EnergyUnitType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/attend", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The vulnerability requires attention from the organization's internal, supervisory-level individuals. Necessary actions include requesting assistance or information about the vulnerability, and may involve publishing a notification either internally and/or externally. CISA recommends remediating Attend vulnerabilities sooner than standard update timelines.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ProfileIdentifierType/service", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual", "globalId", "", ""]
