["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isci", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "International Standard Collection Identifier (ISCI) is a variable-length identifier standardized by [ISO 27730](https://www.iso.org/standard/44293.html) for identifying collections held by libraries, archives, museums, and other memory institutions. It consists of two parts: the identifier for the assigning organization (an ISIL) enclosed in square brackets, followed by a local collection identifier string (e.g., `[FR-751041001]Casadesus1`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N63f68edff6d64ca8b5b02c3a281c7bd3", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/autonomous", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Conducting controlled tests, experiments or simulations to verify that specific requirements regarding performance, functionality, robustness, etc. are met.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/created", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Identifies when the Element was originally created.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
